       '2024-12-05'::date, '2024-12-31'::date,
       20.37, 62.43,
       jsonb_build_object('backfilled', true, 'source', 'signed agreement + post-installation savings report',
                          'note', 'Commissioned before this system existed — CON-16 eligibility was never assessed.',
                          'deviations', '["eligibility-never-assessed", "dates-inferred-from-readings", "benchmark-single-demo", "benchmark-adjusted-for-excluded-devices", "two-versions-of-the-demo-report", "report-contradicts-its-own-table"]'::jsonb,
                          'basisNote', '42 tube lights at 20W and 5 surface lights at 18W, all running 24h; theoretical 22.32 kWh/day against a measured 20.37. TWO of the five surface lights were not replaced, and their theoretical 0.86 kWh/day (2 x 18 x 24 / 1000) comes off both sides - CON-16''s excluded-device rule, by theoretical load, as at Aditya Mega City and Arihant Arden. So 20.37 - 0.86 = 19.51 before and 8.19 - 0.86 = 7.33 after, giving 12.18/19.51 = 62.4295%, the agreed 62.43%. The measured whole-circuit ratio is 59.7938%, which is why the benchmark is an override. TWO VERSIONS OF THIS REPORT EXIST. The copy attached to the SIGNED agreement deducts 0.86 and states 62.43%; another revision deducts 2.16 (all five surface lights) and states 66.88%, and reports the whole-month average as 8.19 where the signed copy says 8.21. The signed copy governs. NOTE: this corrects an earlier reading recorded in PROJECT_CONTEXT, which took all five surface lights as unreplaced and put the circuit at 66.89%. Both versions'' conclusions say ''39 motion-enabled tube lights'' and ''62.60%'', matching neither their own findings (42 tube lights) nor their own savings arithmetic. Both tables reproduce their stated averages: 5 pre days 06-10 Dec 2024 average 20.3680 against 20.37, 11 post days 01-11 Jan 2025 average 8.1882 against 8.19. Neither date is stated: meter install taken as the day before the first pre-install reading (06 Dec 2024), replacement as the day before the post-install readings start (01 Jan 2025).'),
       a.id, now()
FROM societies s, admin_users a WHERE s.name = 'Gaur Saundaryam' AND a.id = 'sys-data-import' ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
